---
/**
 * Specification index (MASTER_ROADMAP M7). States the authority model and
 * lists the published versions. The site never becomes a second source of
 * protocol truth: everything under /spec/v<N>/ is generated from the canonical
 * snapshot and names its commit.
 */
import MaturityBadge from '../../components/MaturityBadge.astro';
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { SHORT_COMMIT, SPEC_VERSION, meta, sourceUrl } from '../../content-engine/models/protocol';
import { SPEC_TOPICS } from '../../lib/spec';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Specification"
  tag="/spec/"
  description="The SAIPEN protocol specification: authority model, published versions and the generated reference pages."
>
  <h1>Specification</h1>
  <p><MaturityBadge level="stable" note={`reference generated from SAIPEN ${meta.version} @ ${SHORT_COMMIT}`} /></p>

  <aside class="callout callout--authority">
    <p class="callout__label">Authority</p>
    <p>
      The normative SAIPEN specification is the
      <a href={meta.repository} rel="noopener" data-external>SAIPEN repository</a>:
      <a href={sourceUrl('SPEC.md')} rel="noopener" data-external>SPEC.md</a> for the design and guarantees,
      <a href={sourceUrl('saipen/CORE.md')} rel="noopener" data-external>saipen/CORE.md</a> and its owner modules
      for normative behaviour, and
      <a href={sourceUrl('saipen/REGISTRY.json')} rel="noopener" data-external>saipen/REGISTRY.json</a> for the
      closed machine vocabulary. The pages below render that registry; on any disagreement, the repository wins.
    </p>
  </aside>

  <h2>Published versions</h2>
  <div class="wide-scroll">
    <table class="w-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Version</th>
          <th scope="col">Status</th>
          <th scope="col">Generated from</th>
          <th scope="col">Permanent URL</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">{SPEC_VERSION}</th>
          <td><MaturityBadge level="stable" /></td>
          <td>
            SAIPEN {meta.version} @ <a href={`${meta.repository}/tree/${meta.commit}`} rel="noopener" data-external>{SHORT_COMMIT}</a>
          </td>
          <td><a href={`/spec/${SPEC_VERSION}/`}>/spec/{SPEC_VERSION}/</a></td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="w-panel__note">
    <a href="/spec/latest/">/spec/latest/</a> always redirects to the newest major; link to the versioned URL when the
    meaning must not change.
  </p>

  <h2>Reference pages ({SPEC_VERSION})</h2>
  <dl class="doclist">
    {
      SPEC_TOPICS.map((t) => (
        <>
          <dt>
            <a href={`/spec/${SPEC_VERSION}/${t.slug}/`}>{t.title}</a>
          </dt>
          <dd>{t.description}</dd>
        </>
      ))
    }
  </dl>

  <h2>Machine-readable</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href={`/spec/${SPEC_VERSION}/registry.json`}>/spec/{SPEC_VERSION}/registry.json</a> — the closed protocol vocabulary</li>
    <li><a href={`/spec/${SPEC_VERSION}/state.schema.json`}>/spec/{SPEC_VERSION}/state.schema.json</a> — the STATE.md JSON Schema</li>
    <li><a href={`/spec/${SPEC_VERSION}/adapters.json`}>/spec/{SPEC_VERSION}/adapters.json</a> — host adapters and declared enforcement</li>
    <li><a href="/llms.txt">/llms.txt</a> — an index of this site for agents</li>
  </ul>
</SiteLayout>
